{"content_hash": "0a5a27197e8cba23", "version_id": 136, "article_id": 14, "level_code": "ja_n5", "lang": "ja", "level": 1, "level_label": "N5 初級", "title": "女王が「元気な人」ジェフリー・アーチャーをほめる", "title_zh": "女王称赞“精力充沛”的杰弗里·阿彻", "topic": "culture", "source": "bbc_culture", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm3wvq4jj64yo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/3d1d/live/ac47b690-c188-11f1-83c7-97e75190a976.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 259, "reading_minutes": 0.9, "lead": "イギリスの作家ジェフリー・アーチャーさんが86さいでなくなりました。女王カミラは、アーチャーさんをほめることばを出しました。", "lead_zh": "英国作家杰弗里·阿彻去世，享年86岁。卡米拉女王发表声明，称赞了阿彻。", "preview": "アーチャーさんは、10月6日に亡くなりました。86さいでした。女王カミラは「悲しいです」と言いました。アーチャーさんは、たくさんの本を書きました。300万さつより多く売れました。", "preview_zh": "阿彻于10月6日去世，享年86岁。卡米拉女王表示“很悲伤”。阿彻写了很多书，销量超过300万册。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 126, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e099b16/content/audio/14/ja_n5.mp3", "duration": 60.163, "size_bytes": 364752, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 186, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e099b16/content/data/versions/136.json", "paragraphs": ["アーチャーさんは、10月6日に亡くなりました。86さいでした。女王カミラは「悲しいです」と言いました。アーチャーさんは、たくさんの本を書きました。300万さつより多く売れました。", "アーチャーさんは、政治家でした。保守党の議員でした。2001年、うそをついたため、刑務所に入りました。4年間、刑務所にいました。2003年に出ました。", "女王は「アーチャーさんは、とても元気な人でした」と言いました。アーチャーさんの本は、とても人気がありました。最後の本は、10月6日に出ました。", "アーチャーさんは、妻のメアリーさんと60年、結婚していました。子どもが2人、まごが5人います。アーチャーさんは、家で静かに亡くなりました。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["阿彻于10月6日去世，享年86岁。卡米拉女王表示“很悲伤”。阿彻写了很多书，销量超过300万册。", "阿彻曾是政治家，是保守党议员。2001年，他因说谎而入狱，在监狱待了4年，2003年出狱。", "女王说：“阿彻是个非常精力充沛的人。”阿彻的书非常受欢迎。他的最后一本书于10月6日出版。", "阿彻与妻子玛丽结婚60年，有两个孩子、五个孙辈。阿彻在家中安详离世。"], "body": "アーチャーさんは、10月6日に亡くなりました。86さいでした。女王カミラは「悲しいです」と言いました。アーチャーさんは、たくさんの本を書きました。300万さつより多く売れました。\n\nアーチャーさんは、政治家でした。保守党の議員でした。2001年、うそをついたため、刑務所に入りました。4年間、刑務所にいました。2003年に出ました。\n\n女王は「アーチャーさんは、とても元気な人でした」と言いました。アーチャーさんの本は、とても人気がありました。最後の本は、10月6日に出ました。\n\nアーチャーさんは、妻のメアリーさんと60年、結婚していました。子どもが2人、まごが5人います。アーチャーさんは、家で静かに亡くなりました。", "body_zh": "阿彻于10月6日去世，享年86岁。卡米拉女王表示“很悲伤”。阿彻写了很多书，销量超过300万册。\n\n阿彻曾是政治家，是保守党议员。2001年，他因说谎而入狱，在监狱待了4年，2003年出狱。\n\n女王说：“阿彻是个非常精力充沛的人。”阿彻的书非常受欢迎。他的最后一本书于10月6日出版。\n\n阿彻与妻子玛丽结婚60年，有两个孩子、五个孙辈。阿彻在家中安详离世。", "text": "アーチャーさんは、10月6日に亡くなりました。86さいでした。女王カミラは「悲しいです」と言いました。アーチャーさんは、たくさんの本を書きました。300万さつより多く売れました。 アーチャーさんは、政治家でした。保守党の議員でした。2001年、うそをついたため、刑務所に入りました。4年間、刑務所にいました。2003年に出ました。 女王は「アーチャーさんは、とても元気な人でした」と言いました。アーチャーさんの本は、とても人気がありました。最後の本は、10月6日に出ました。 アーチャーさんは、妻のメアリーさんと60年、結婚していました。子どもが2人、まごが5人います。アーチャーさんは、家で静かに亡くなりました。", "vocab": [{"word": "作家", "pos": "noun", "zh": "作家", "note": ""}, {"word": "亡くなる", "pos": "verb", "zh": "去世", "note": "礼貌说法"}, {"word": "女王", "pos": "noun", "zh": "女王", "note": ""}, {"word": "本", "pos": "noun", "zh": "书", "note": ""}, {"word": "政治家", "pos": "noun", "zh": "政治家", "note": ""}, {"word": "刑務所", "pos": "noun", "zh": "监狱", "note": ""}, {"word": "結婚", "pos": "noun", "zh": "结婚", "note": ""}, {"word": "静か", "pos": "adj", "zh": "安静", "note": "静かに＝安静地"}], "title_original": "Queen pays tribute to 'irrepressible' Jeffrey Archer", "summary_original": "The bestselling author and former politician died on Monday at the age of 86.", "body_original": "Queen pays tribute to 'irrepressible' Jeffrey Archer\nBy\nEmma Saunders\n,\nCulture reporter\nand\nHenry Moore\nPublished\n6 October 2026\nQueen Camilla has paid tribute to the bestselling author and former politician Jeffrey Archer, who has died at the age of 86.\n\"Seldom does an author get to live a life as rich, varied and colourful as any of the characters in their books, or with as many surprising plot twists,\" the Queen said in a statement.\nShe added that Archer was \"not without flaw\", but that \"friends will recall him as an irrepressible life force through all the many differing chapters of his life\".\nThe former Conservative MP was jailed for perjury in 2001 after being found guilty of lying and cheating in his 1987 libel case against the Daily Star.\nThe Queen said he was \"an exception to the end\" and that it was \"with sadness that I learned of his death yesterday, on the eve of publication of his final work and so soon after appearing at my Queen's Reading Room Festival\".\nArcher was a supporter of the Queen's Reading Room charity.\n\"My sympathies go to Mary and the family at this time of sorrow. I hope it may be some consolation for them to know what pleasure Jeffrey brought to me and to so many millions of readers through the pages of his works.\n\"Wherever the next page turns to, I trust there will be champagne and Shepherd's Pie in abundance. Camilla R.\"\nArcher's parties were known for serving champagne and shepherd's pie to guests.\nFalse alibi\nArcher sold more than 300 million books in his five-decade writing career, including the Clifton Chronicles and Kane and Abel, and often set the novels in his home town of Wellington, Somerset.\nIn a statement, Archer's publisher HarperCollins said the author died \"suddenly and peacefully at home\" on Monday between writing sessions.\nArcher was born in north London in 1940 but soon moved to Weston-super-Mare in Somerset and in 1969, Archer was elected MP for the Lincolnshire constituency of Louth.\nHe served as an MP for five years before becoming Conservative Party deputy chairman.\nHe moved to the House of Lords in 1992 but was jailed for four years for perjury and perverting the course of justice in 2001.\nHe was found to have lied in libel action he had brought against the Daily Star newspaper, in which he was awarded £500,000 in damages.\nThe Star had alleged Archer had slept with a sex worker.\nThe peer was found by the court to have perverted the course of justice by asking a former friend to give him a false alibi and producing fake diary entries to back up his story.\nHe was also found to have perjured himself on oath during the libel trial.\nHe was released from jail in 2003 and returned to the House of Lords until he retired in 2024.\nConservative Party leader Kemi Badenoch described Archer's death as \"devastating news\".\n\"We will miss him very much,\" she told BBC Breakfast on Tuesday, adding that he had texted her earlier on Monday.\nBadenoch said he was \"very much loved by the Conservative family\", adding: \"I'm glad that I saw him recently.\"\nSpeaking about what she described as \"other parts of his life\", she said: \"He did serve his time, he made amends, and he wanted to do a lot of good in the world.\"\nFormer Conservative prime minister Sir John Major said \"we have lost a man who lived one of the most remarkable lives of our age\", and that he will be \"much missed – and long remembered\".\nArcher's last novel, Adam and Eve, was released on Tuesday.\nBroadcaster Gyles Brandreth told BBC Breakfast that he was with Archer on Sunday. \"I mean, literally 72 hours ago, doing a show in the West End of London celebrating this book, the publication, and he was in great form.\n\"He didn't really acknowledge that he'd changed much since being in prison, but I think he became a nicer person in some ways, a gentler, a milder person after the prison experience.\"\nFormer Conservative Party leader Iain Duncan Smith described Archer as \"a remarkable man who did everything at full bore\", adding: \"There were simply no half measures with him.\"\nOther former ministers also paid tribute. Sajid Javid said Archer had been a \"dear friend\", while Sir Jeremy Hunt said Archer had \"showed enormous kindness with his advice about how to become a writer\".\nJames Cleverly said the author and politician had been \"a huge personality and fantastic storyteller\", and that he had been very supportive when his wife Suzie was recovering from cancer.\nReform UK member and former Conservative minister Nadim Zahawi, wrote: \"Jeffrey Archer was a dear friend and an extraordinary human being. His gift for storytelling was matched by his wit, warmth and boundless energy. Life was never dull in Jeffrey's company.\"\nAuthor and former politician Jeffrey Archer dies aged 86\nPublished\n15 hours ago\nJeffrey Archer: bestselling novelist whose political career ended in scandal\nPublished\n1 day ago\nArcher 'nostalgic' about Somerset before death\nPublished\n14 hours ago\nLast week, Archer returned to his former school to promote his last book.\n\"It's wonderful to come back. What I got a real thrill about when I was walking towards the library is seeing the young boys and girls and thinking, 'that's the next generation',\" Archer said at Wellington School.\nArcher had been due to attend the Cheltenham Literature Festival on Saturday to discuss his final novel.\nHe and his wife Mary had celebrated their 60th wedding anniversary this year, HarperCollins said.\nThe couple have two sons and five grandchildren.\nRelated topics\nQueen Camilla\nUK Royal Family\nLiterature\nBooks", "fetched_at": "2026-10-07T00:55:38.692252", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "アーチャー", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.588, "sm": 125, "em": 587, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "さん", "s": 0.6, "e": 0.837, "sm": 600, "em": 837, "cs": 5, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "は", "s": 0.85, "e": 1.125, "sm": 850, "em": 1125, "cs": 7, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "、", "s": 1.125, "e": 1.4, "sm": 1125, "em": 1400, "cs": 8, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "10", "s": 1.4, "e": 1.75, "sm": 1400, "em": 1749, "cs": 9, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "月", "s": 1.75, "e": 1.925, "sm": 1749, "em": 1924, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "6", "s": 1.938, "e": 2.087, "sm": 1937, "em": 2087, "cs": 12, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "日", "s": 2.087, "e": 2.237, "sm": 2087, "em": 2237, "cs": 13, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "に", "s": 2.25, "e": 2.4, "sm": 2250, "em": 2400, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "亡くなり", "s": 2.413, "e": 2.85, "sm": 2412, "em": 2850, "cs": 15, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "まし", "s": 2.862, "e": 3.0